# Line-ending normalisation for the build tooling. Without this the same script
# checks out with different bytes per platform, and a shell script that acquires
# CRLF fails on Linux/macOS.

# The POSIX wrapper script must stay LF: a CRLF in mvnw makes the shebang invalid.
/mvnw text eol=lf

# Windows batch scripts must stay CRLF, because cmd.exe misparses LF-only .cmd
# files in some edge cases.
*.cmd text eol=crlf
